<title>USA: No damaging cold in sight for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>No damaging cold in sight for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>No damaging cold is in sight for Brazil's coffee-growing areas for the next five days, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp (WSC) said on Friday.</p>
<p>WSC forecast scattered light to locally moderate showers in the south on Friday and in all areas on Saturday, with coverage of 40-50 percent. Temperatures will be near to above normal, and overnight lows of mostly 53-65 degrees F are likely.</p>
<p>The outlook calls for a chance of a few light showers in the south on Sunday, but mostly dry weather on Monday-Tuesday. Temperatures will be near to above normal.</p>
<p>East-central Brazil was dry on Thursday, with highs of 77-86 and lows of 50-63.</p>
</text>
